From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: csiphy: Feed several CSIDs without a clock mux

Only CSIPHYs with a clock mux, on the older SoCs, drive a single CSID.
Elsewhere each CSID selects its PHY, so let the source pad link to
several CSIDs, for instance two pixel paths that share a frame wider
than one IFE can take.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
index 539ac4888..55c15caeb 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy.c
@@ -728,12 +728,17 @@ static int csiphy_link_setup(struct media_entity *entity,
 		struct csiphy_device *csiphy;
 		struct csid_device *csid;
 
-		if (media_pad_remote_pad_first(local))
-			return -EBUSY;
-
 		sd = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(entity);
 		csiphy = v4l2_get_subdevdata(sd);
 
+		/*
+		 * A CSIPHY with a clock mux drives one CSID. Without it, each
+		 * CSID selects its PHY and several can take the same stream,
+		 * e.g. two pixel paths sharing a wide frame.
+		 */
+		if (csiphy->base_clk_mux && media_pad_remote_pad_first(local))
+			return -EBUSY;
+
 		sd = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(remote->entity);
 		csid = v4l2_get_subdevdata(sd);
 
